/**
 * The Partition of India, 1947 — Dossier topic exhibit.
 *
 * Research rules followed here:
 *  - every claim has >=1 source and an honest confidence grade; contested/tradition claims carry a note;
 *  - the exhibit does not take a nationalist side: Congress, the Muslim League, the British, the princely
 *    rulers, and Hindu, Muslim, Sikh and other communities are each described by what the sources show;
 *  - death tolls, displacement and abduction figures are shown as ranges and graded contested;
 *  - direct quotation appears only where the exact wording was read in a fetched source:
 *      the Radcliffe reports (Gazette of India Extraordinary, 17 Aug 1947, via Wikisource),
 *      the Indian Independence Act 1947 (legislation.gov.uk), the Lahore Resolution (indiaofthepast.org),
 *      Jinnah's 11 Aug 1947 address (Pritchett's transcription), and Nehru's "Tryst with Destiny" (Wikisource);
 *      survivor testimony is limited to one short phrase as printed by Bhalla (NEH, 2022);
 *  - this is a topic dossier, so `characters` is empty and no identifiable person is invented;
 *    distressing photographs are not used, and every image of crowds or refugees is gated by minDepth;
 *  - the evidence behind each source is recorded in docs/dossier/partition-research-notes.md.
 */
